# Macros named *_MAX_* or *_LIMIT* that are not limits a user can reach, so they have no row in SIFT_LIMITS (src/core/limits.h).
# NAME, a tab, the reason. scripts/gen-limits.sh --check fails for a macro that is neither here nor a row, and for a line whose macro is gone.
# A bound that a user can reach gets a row, not a line here.
CHUNK_MAX_N	sanity bound on the row count a decoder reads from a chunk: a corruption check
COL_MAX_WIDE	array size that mirrors wide_conjuncts (SIFT_AGG_MAX_WIDE)
ESTIMATE_MEMO_MAX_KEY	size of the key of a planner memo: an internal cache bound with no visible effect
LOOKCACHE_MAX_BLOCKS	derived from the lookup cache budget (sift.agg_lookup_cache_kb)
MERGE_MAX_BYTES	no caller left: delete it in a cleanup
ORDER_MAX_ROWS	the most rows of a key-cut unit, the maximum of key_cut_rows (the directory of a unit is read with the head of its record)
PAGG_MAX_TUPLES	decoder bound for a rollup blob (a corruption check), derived from rollup_tuples
POOL_MAX_BLOCKS	size of the CREATE INDEX buffer pool, kept so that addresses stay below 2^32 (sift.test_pool_blocks lowers it)
PROBE_MAX_ENTRIES	size of the table of one planner probe: an internal bound with no visible effect
SIFT_AGG_MAX_PARAMS	derived array size of the executor parameters
SIFT_ALLOC_MAX_LOCKED	invariant of the block allocator, not reachable by valid input
SIFT_COLSTUB_MAX_STR	test-only stub source (SIFT_TESTING)
SIFT_COL_FORMAT_MAX_READ	the newest column format minor this build reads: a version, not a size
SIFT_COL_MAX_LANES	array size of the lanes of one numeric leaf
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_KEYS	keys of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_ROWS	rows of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_FOLD_MAX_EXPAND	characters one character expands to in case folding: a property of the Unicode tables
SIFT_MAX_EXTENTS	derived from the page layout (extents of a segment header)
SIFT_MAX_OFF	width of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MAX_OFFSET	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_MAX_REBINDS	size of the table of kernel rebind callbacks
SIFT_MAX_W	words of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_FANIN	merge policy: segments one merge reads at a time
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_SEGMENTS	merge policy: more directory entries than this start a merge
SIFT_NUM_MAX_DIGITS	the same limit as wide_digits, counted by the planner
SIFT_SRC_MAX_DIMS	planner-side array size of the dimensions of a source, above cube_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_MEAS	planner-side array size that mirrors cube_measures
SIFT_SRC_MAX_RDIMS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollup_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_ROLLUPS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollups
SIFT_TBL_MAX_OFF	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_TBL_MAX_WBUF_PAGES	array size of the page list of one write buffer: see write_buffer_kb and tx_write_buffers
SIFT_TBL_ROW_MAX_INLINE	a sift_table row above half a page goes to overflow pages: a layout threshold, not a limit
SIFT_VK_MAX_GROUPS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_PRED	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_RS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_SLOTS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_SUM	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
SIFT_VK_MAX_UNITS	shader job layout of the opt-in Vulkan backend
VK_MAX_MEMORY_HEAPS	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_MEMORY_TYPES	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_NAME_SIZE	constant of the Vulkan API
